format session-log-v1
stamp 20260822.043742
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The roster that named more than it ran
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, council rota one row, send.
think Standfast opened the lap and this time it did not run clear. `tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_witness.rish` -- the guard that reads every REDS row for its three fields -- refused with verdict=incomplete_rows, naming the REDS %128 CLOSED row as thin. Reading the scan explained why: a closure note that claims no fields must name its proof instead, matching GREEN or "on metal" or "Released", because a fix closes on a witness on metal and never on a claim. The %128 closure named none of them, and honestly so -- it closed by editing prose.
think The root was found by bisecting rather than by reasoning. Running the scan against `git show <nib>:crux/REDS.md` for the four commits behind HEAD dated it exactly: ok at 64d4f2855b, incomplete_rows from ac68074042 onward -- the very commit that closed REDS %128. Three further lifts landed on top of it and all four rode signed to both remotes, while every lap's Standfast reported the era suite GREEN.
think The structural cause is a roster gap. Two guards watch crux/REDS.md and only one is rostered: `reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish` counts the spine and checks the headline and is era rung 9; `reds_ledger_witness.rish` reads every row for completeness and sits on no roster at all. The rung's own line reads "the reds ledger itself", so the roster promised the whole subject and delivered half of it -- REDS %102's shape one level up, since that row asked a single witness to cover its whole subject and this one asks a roster to.
think REDS %128 had booked a prevention and never built it: a quantity a sentence asserts about the diff belongs in the same sentence as the command that reads it back. So the closure earns its proof by building that guard rather than by rewording. `tools/fixtures/ladder_stub_length_scan.sh` spans the enclosing function of every `return ladder_checks.` call across the 79 caravan modules, counts the pure delegating stubs -- those whose whole body is that single return -- and reports the measured minimum.
think The measurement is real rather than definitional. 2,841 delegating return lines stand across the ladder; only 2,141 of them sit in pure stubs, and the other 700 are functions that do their own work before delegating, spanning 5 to 19 lines. The reported minimum is 3, and a stub that grew an invariant comment or a multi-line signature would move it, so the number can go stale and say so on the lap it does.
think The guard refused the tree on its first honest run, and the refusal was instructive rather than correct. Holding session-logs/README.md to today's disk reddened on two index rows that truthfully describe a FIVE-line stub from the `link` arc of 20260820, a shape whose 612 stubs have since left the ladder. That is history, not drift. The scope narrowed to crux/REMEMBER.md -- the card that speaks as now -- on the line the tree already draws: a file whose basename carries a one-clock stamp is testimony, and the log index is testimony's face.
think One bug in the scan was caught by disbelieving its own calm. It first answered claims=0 while the card plainly wrote "three-line stub", because a quoted "${@:-$default}" collapses two paths into one word and reads neither. A scan answering zero about a surface it never opened is the exact blindness the scan exists to refuse, so the fix carries that reason in a comment beside it.
obs The repair is three acts and each closed on metal. Era rung 9 now runs both ledger halves and asserts both. Rung 10 joins with `tools/ladder_stub_length_witness.rish`, and the suite renumbers 1/9 through 9/9 to 1/10 through 10/10 in the same pass, since a rung count carried in prose drifts the moment a rung is added -- %127's headline shape again. The whole suite ran ten rungs GREEN end to end.
obs The living pin passed its bound as row %129 landed -- 26,373 bytes against 24,576 -- and the guard named its own remedy. The elder closures for %81, %83, %84, %98 folded to `crux/archive/REDS-elder-closures-rows-81-98.md`, every byte kept, bringing the pin to 19,799. The headline then answered to the spine: total and span 128 to 129, remainder 108 to 109, all three read off the monotone witness rather than typed from a glance.
obs Council rota, row one -- Air and Saturn, law and boundary -- and it read as though written for this lap. Conway's Law says the architecture copies the communication structure, and here the roster IS the channel between sessions: a guard on no roster is a message never sent forward, which is why it stood red for four commits with nobody to notice. Single-strandedness names the same fault from the other side -- one subject, two guards, coverage braided across two places with only one of them read. TAME core's own line closes it: a fix is closed by a witness on metal, never a claim.
obs The %128 CLOSED row gains a dated proof clause rather than a rewrite of what it originally said. The closure that rested on a prose edit stays visible as exactly that, and the guard that finally proves it sits beside it, named and stamped.
loom witness=glow_tend_era_suite rungs=10 verdict=GREEN
loom scan=ladder_stub_length pure_stubs=2141 stub_lines=3 delegating_returns=2841 modules=79 claims=2 claims_adrift=0
loom pin=crux/REDS.md bytes_before=26373 bytes_after=19799 bound=24576 rows_folded=4
loom spine=reds_ledger_monotone rows=129 gaps_or_dupes=0 disagreements=0
file tools/fixtures/ladder_stub_length_scan.sh the prevention REDS %128 booked -- measures the stub off disk, holds the live card to it, refuses blindness by name
file tools/ladder_stub_length_witness.rish the witness over it, both refusals proven on generated controls before the tree is read
file tools/glow_tend_era_suite.rish rung 9 runs both ledger halves, rung 10 runs the stub guard, and the ten rungs are renumbered in the same pass
file crux/REDS.md row %129 booked and closed, the %128 closure given its proof clause, the headline answering the measured spine
file crux/archive/REDS-elder-closures-rows-81-98.md four elder closures folded whole so the living pin returns under its bound
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live card refilled with what this lap closed and what the ladder queue holds next
recommend keep-going recant_published at thirty-seven rungs by twenty lines -- 612 by realized fall, one identical body in every rung and the same five contract symbols already public throughout, so it is the head that widens nothing and it closes the glyph-note family. The arithmetic is now guarded rather than asserted: era rung 10 measures the three-line stub off disk every lap and refuses a card that says otherwise. renew_path (720) and ask_path (660) each widen thirty-one declarations; choose_pass (630) reaches three private neighbors.
